\begin{remark}
\label{rem:asymmetric}
Theorem~\ref{thm:bias_identity} does not require~(A2).
For arbitrary asymmetric CMs, the product form $\mathrm{bias}(z, s) = \Delta\tau \cdot [B_s]_{z,1}$ holds exactly with $B_s = M_{\mathrm{global}}^{-1} M_s - I$, since $B_s \mathbf{1} = \mathbf{0}$ follows from stochasticity alone; (A2) only simplifies $[B_s]_{z,1}$ to the scalar $\pm \delta_s / (1{-}2\bar{\pi})$.
Under asymmetric errors, the diagnostic (Proposition~\ref{prop:debiasing_hurts}) with $\pi_s = (\mathrm{FPR}_s + \mathrm{FNR}_s)/2$ achieves AUC $= 0.96$ across 48 configurations and correctly identifies all harmed subgroups across 8 semi-real LLM CMs (Appendix~\ref{app:asymmetric}).
\end{remark}

